course: dictionary
lesson: 12841
title: Enclosed: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Look at the words near «enclosed» for clues. «The goats were kept in an enclosed field, with a high fence all the way round.» The fence and all the way round tell you enclosed means surrounded on every side.
explain: «Please find enclosed my drawing of the castle.» Here enclosed means put inside an envelope or parcel with a letter. Please find and the formal tone are your clues. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Please find put inside my drawing" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Enclosed is also the past form of enclose, so it can tell you what someone already did: «Dad enclosed the vegetable patch with wooden posts last week.» Enclose is the action; enclosed is the action in the past. Ask yourself: is something surrounded, or did someone do something?
fact: Enclosed means surrounded on all sides by walls, a fence or something else.
fact: Enclosed can also mean put inside an envelope or parcel, usually with a letter.
fact: «Please find enclosed» is a formal phrase in letters, meaning "I have put this inside for you".
fact: Enclosed is the past form of enclose: to put a fence or wall around something.
fact: In maths, an enclosed shape is a closed shape with no gaps, so you can find its area.
exercise: «The goats were kept in an enclosed field behind a high fence.» What does enclosed mean here? | Lost and far from home | Put inside an envelope | *Surrounded on all sides by a fence | Sold at the market
exercise: «Please find enclosed the photo of our class trip.» What does enclosed mean here? | Surrounded by a wall | Rolled up and thrown away | *Put inside the envelope with the letter | Hidden under the bed
exercise: «Dad enclosed the garden with a wooden fence.» What did Dad do? | Took the fence down | *Put a fence around the garden | Ate his lunch in the garden | Painted the fence blue
test: In maths, what is an enclosed shape? | A shape that is always round | A shape you cannot measure | *A closed shape with no gaps | A shape with gaps in it
test: Nadia writes, «Please find enclosed my homework.» Where is the homework? | In her school bag | On the table | Lost in the post | *Inside the envelope with her letter
exam: Which sentence uses enclosed to mean put inside? | Ben walked around the enclosed yard | Ben enclosed his friends in a song | Ben ate an enclosed sandwich | *Ben enclosed a stamped card in the parcel
